# Agent efficiency

## Before coding

- Use **Ask mode** for questions; **Agent mode** only for implementation.
- Prefer **@file** / **@folder** in the user prompt over "search the whole repo."
- Read `AGENTS.md` once per task — do not re-derive repo structure from scratch.

## During coding

- **Grep** for symbols; **Read** only files you will edit or that define the API you call.
- Never read `node_modules/`, `dist/`, or lockfiles unless debugging install issues.
- Parallel tool calls for independent reads; avoid sequential exploration loops.
- One concern per turn: fix → test → report; don't re-explain the entire architecture.
- Match existing style in the **same directory**; don't refactor unrelated code.

## Verification (pick ONE)

| Change type | Command |
|-------------|---------|
| RBAC / gateway routes | `cd backend && npm run test:rbac` |
| Auth / invites | `npm run test:auth:live --prefix backend/gateway` |
| Tenant / isolation | `npm run test:tenancy --prefix backend/gateway` |
| MDM | `cd backend && npm run test:mdm` |
| Drivers | `cd backend && npm run test:drivers` |
| Single service unit test | `npm test --prefix backend/services/<name>-service` |

## Avoid (wastes tokens)

- Reading every `*-COMPLETE.md` when one chapter applies
- Launching broad **Task/explore** subagents for a single known file
- Generating long markdown docs the user didn't request
- Re-running full `start:dev` when only one service changed
- Duplicating troubleshooting the user already resolved in the same thread
